        "title": "Fashion Design Principles - Constraint Satisfaction in Cloth",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Every garment is a solution to a constraint-satisfaction problem. The body is the input. The occasion is the requirement. The fabric is the constraint. The silhouette is the output. Good design satisfies all four simultaneously; great design makes you forget the constraints existed."
